---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const seo = {
  title: "AI | Lauro",
  description: "My current stance on AI (and how it's used on this website)",
};
---

<Page seo={seo}>
  <h1>My stance on AI</h1>

  <p>
    Everything I write and create here is mainly made by me. I don't use AI to write my blog posts for me and don't plan to change it.
    But I feel it's fair for those who are completely against LLMs to disclose that I do use Claude Code
    for manual development tasks using Anthropic's models.
  </p>

  <p>
    Personally, I'm not against generative AI by itself, although I'm against many things that are powered by generative AI
    and I don't like how these companies operate. But that's my stance on every single major company, AI or not.
  </p>

  <p>
    I consider LLMs are a tool that I have gotten used to work with, because my line of work currently requires that.
    It allows me to focus on what's the important part of my creations while all the code-writting is handed to the agents.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    I use it for development tasks, but only manual work: things like upgrading dependencies, moving between tools and implementing changes I've already
    decided on.
  </p>

  <p>
    Sometimes I also use Grammarly for English grammar corrections, but I don't use it to generate new text.
  </p>

  <p>
    Otherwise, every blog posts (ideas and words), the photos, lists, decisions about what this website says, looks and feels, is completely made by me.
  </p>

  <p>Posts carry this badge at the bottom, as a reminder:</p>

  <p>
    <a class="not-ai" href="https://notbyai.fyi/" target="_blank">
      <Image
        src="/assets/notAI.png"
        alt="Written by a human, not by AI"
        width={70}
        height={18}
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </a>
  </p>

  <p>I don't like reading AI texts, so I won't have you go through what I go through daily at work.</p>

  <p>
    The code of this website is <a href="https://github.com/lsfgrd/lauro.xyz" target="_blank"> public on GitHub</a>, if you're curious about how it's built.
  </p>

  <p>
    <small>Last updated: 18/10/2026</small>
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .not-ai::after {
    content: none !important;
  }
</style>
